2. गम् (occurring only in gen. and abl. गमस्), Ved.
the earth; [cf. क्षम्: cf. also Gr. γῆ; Zend zem;
Lith. zemie; Slav. zemlje; Russ. zemlu.]

गामिन्, ई, इनी, इ, going, moving on, or in, or
towards, or in any peculiar manner, &c.; going to,
having intercourse with; reaching to, extending to;
coming to one's share, due; attaining, obtaining;
directed towards; relating to; [cf. अग्र-गामिन्,
अन्त-ग्˚, अन्य-ग्˚, आशु-ग्˚, ऋतु-ग्˚, काम-ग्˚.]
